{"t": 509.28, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "VoltageDoubler_Clamp", "rationale": "The FBR design is very close to meeting the requirements but fails on S2 and S4 because the open-circuit voltage (Voc) of the piezo is too low to overcome the diode drops and the load. A voltage doubler (charge pump) is used here to boost the output voltage, ensuring Vout remains above 1.8V even for the weak excitation (S4) and heavy load (S2). A Zener diode (DZ33) is added to clamp the output to 3.3V, preventing the high-excitation case (S3) from exceeding the load's absolute maximum of 3.6V. Two capacitors are used: one as the flying capacitor for the doubling action and one as the storage capacitor to minimize ripple.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "VoltageDoubler_Clamp", "rationale": "The FBR design is very close to meeting the requirements but fails on S2 and S4 because the open-circuit voltage (Voc) of the piezo is too low to overcome the diode drops and the load. A voltage doubler (charge pump) is used here to boost the output voltage, ensuring Vout remains above 1.8V even for the weak excitation (S4) and heavy load (S2). A Zener diode (DZ33) is added to clamp the output to 3.3V, preventing the high-excitation case (S3) from exceeding the load's absolute maximum of 3.6V. Two capacitors are used: one as the flying capacitor for the doubling action and one as the storage capacitor to minimize ripple.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "n1"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["n1", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C2", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 2.2e-05}, {"id": "Dz", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
